    "ex-qftmath-x04": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-qft-example-massive-tree-annihilation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $m,M\\geq0$ be the electron and muon rest energies in joules. Let $p_1,p_2$ be future electron/positron energy four-vectors of rest energy $m$, and $k_1,k_2$ future muon/antimuon energy four-vectors of rest energy $M$, with $p_1+p_2=k_1+k_2=P$, $s=P^2>4\\max(m^2,M^2)$, and the algebraic metric $h=(+,-,-,-)$. Use the dimensionless coupling $g=\\sqrt{4\\pi\\alpha}$ from [[def-qft-example-data]]. Adopt only the formal single-photon tree coefficient\n$$\\mathcal M=\\frac{g^2}{s} [\\bar v(p_2)\\gamma^a u(p_1)] [\\bar u(k_1)\\gamma_a v(k_2)],$$\nwith equal weight $1/4$ on the four initial spin-label pairs and a sum over final spin labels. No interacting continuum $S$-matrix or exact QED cross section is assumed.\n\nIn the auxiliary finite-matrix setting of [L1], assume $d\\geq1$, an invertible $K_0$, and the stated covariance of $K_0$ and $V$ under the finite-graph phase action; then the coefficientwise inverse and covariance identities in [L1] hold. Separately stipulate the displayed formal pair-production amplitude above. Its on-shell spin average is\n$$\\overline{|\\mathcal M|^2} =g^4[3-\\beta_e^2-\\beta_\\mu^2 +\\beta_e^2\\beta_\\mu^2\\cos^2\\theta], \\qquad \\beta_e=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{4m^2}{s}}, \\quad \\beta_\\mu=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{4M^2}{s}},$$\nwhere $\\theta$ is the center-of-momentum angle between $p_1$ and $k_1$. The resulting formal differential and total coefficients are\n$$\\frac{d\\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}}}{d\\Omega} =\\frac{\\alpha^2(\\hbar c)^2\\beta_\\mu}{4s\\beta_e} [3-\\beta_e^2-\\beta_\\mu^2+\\beta_e^2\\beta_\\mu^2\\cos^2\\theta],$$\n$$\\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}} =\\frac{\\pi\\alpha^2(\\hbar c)^2}{s}\\frac{\\beta_\\mu}{\\beta_e} [3-\\beta_e^2-\\beta_\\mu^2+\\tfrac13\\beta_e^2\\beta_\\mu^2].$$\nIf $\\delta=4m^2/s\\leq1/2$, the full differential coefficient divided by its $m=0$ value is between $1$ and $1+4\\delta$. This bound concerns only omission of the incoming electron mass in this formal tree coefficient, not loop, soft-radiation, threshold, or empirical errors.\n\nThe same on-shell equations give $P_a\\bar v(p_2)\\gamma^a u(p_1)=0$ and $P_a\\bar u(k_1)\\gamma^a v(k_2)=0$. Thus a propagator term proportional to $P_aP_b$ does not change this specified tree coefficient. These current cancellations are proved locally for all $m,M\\geq0$; the actual QFT-MG03 matrix-Ward carrier supplies only its finite-matrix inverse and covariance interface, not the broader tree-current clauses in the historical Q7 research module.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Setting $\\beta_e=\\beta_\\mu=1$ in [F1] gives $d\\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}}/d\\Omega=\\alpha^2(\\hbar c)^2(1+\\cos^2\\theta)/(4s)$. At $\\theta=0$ this is $\\alpha^2(\\hbar c)^2/(2s)$; at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ it is $\\alpha^2(\\hbar c)^2/(4s)$, so the ratio is $2$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Integrating the same density over the sphere uses $\\int d\\Omega=4\\pi$ and $\\int\\cos^2\\theta\\,d\\Omega=4\\pi/3$, giving $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}}=4\\pi\\alpha^2(\\hbar c)^2/(3s)$, in agreement with [F1]. No count data or continuum scattering operator is introduced.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
            "F1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
